    "summary": "Cloth (aso oke woman&#039;s wrapper) composed of 10 narrow strips of machine cotton, hand sewn together along the selvedges. Each strip is the same, with a group wefr of alternating blue adn white cotton, and a weft of blue cotton only. Each strip has the same text added in supplementary rayon weft, once in white in Yoruba, and once in light blue in Arabic. The individual words are divided by extra motifs, one being of a crocodile, in the same white and light blue rayon thread. The cloth is machine hemmed.",
